{"name":"Mistletoe Kiss","hex":"#98b489","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mistletoe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of numerous hemiparasitic evergreen plants of the order Santalales with white berries that grow in the crowns of apple trees, oaks, and other trees, such as the European mistletoe (Viscum album) and American mistletoe or eastern mistletoe (Phoradendron leucarpum).","A sprig of one such plant used as a Christmas decoration, associated with the custom that a man may kiss any woman standing beneath it."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mistletoe"},{"term":"kiss","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To touch with the lips or press the lips against, usually to show love or affection or passion, or as part of a greeting.","To (cause to) touch lightly or slightly; to come into contact."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A touch with the lips, usually to express love or affection, or as a greeting.","An 'X' mark placed at the end of a letter or other type of message, signifying the bestowal of a kiss from the sender to the receiver."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiss"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mistletoe","blocks":[{"text":"Mistletoe is the common name for obligate hemiparasitic plants in the order Santalales. They are attached to their host tree or shrub by a structure called the haustorium, through which they extract water and nutrients from the host plant. There are hundreds of species which mostly live in tropical regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Viscum_album_2026_G1.jpg/330px-Viscum_album_2026_G1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mistletoe","wikidata":"Q2885646"},{"title":"Kiss","blocks":[{"text":"A kiss is the touching or pressing of one's lips against another person, animal, or object. The cultural connotations associated with kissing vary significantly between different societies and contexts. Depending on the culture and circumstances, a kiss can express a wide range of emotions, such as love, passion, romance, sexual attraction, sexual arousal, affection, respect, a wish for peace or good luck, as well as numerous other meanings. In some situations, kissing takes on the function of a greeting or a ritual, formal, or symbolic gesture indicating religious devotion, institutional respect, or an act of sacramental nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg/330px-Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiss","wikidata":"Q7307"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Mistletoe.jpg/500px-Mistletoe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Mistletoe.jpg/500px-Mistletoe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"European mistletoe growing on an apple tree (Malus domestica); despite the mistletoe's presence, the apple tree is still able to bear fruit.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMistletoe.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Mistleltoe_in_Lebanon.JPG/500px-Mistleltoe_in_Lebanon.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Mistleltoe_in_Lebanon.JPG/1280px-Mistleltoe_in_Lebanon.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Mistleltoe_in_Lebanon.JPG/500px-Mistleltoe_in_Lebanon.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mistletoe in winter","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMistleltoe_in_Lebanon.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Adrien_Barr%C3%A8re14.jpg/250px-Adrien_Barr%C3%A8re14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/33/Adrien_Barr%C3%A8re14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Adrien_Barr%C3%A8re14.jpg/250px-Adrien_Barr%C3%A8re14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Mistletoe Seller by Adrien Barrère","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAdrien_Barr%C3%A8re14.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Christmas_on_the_Western_Front%2C_1914-1918_Q1627.jpg/500px-Christmas_on_the_Western_Front%2C_1914-1918_Q1627.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Christmas_on_the_Western_Front%2C_1914-1918_Q1627.jpg/1280px-Christmas_on_the_Western_Front%2C_1914-1918_Q1627.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Christmas_on_the_Western_Front%2C_1914-1918_Q1627.jpg/500px-Christmas_on_the_Western_Front%2C_1914-1918_Q1627.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Soldiers celebrating Christmas on the western front, December 1916. Each has a sprig of mistletoe attached to his cap.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChristmas_on_the_Western_Front%2C_1914-1918_Q1627.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/USMC-16853.jpg/500px-USMC-16853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/USMC-16853.jpg/1280px-USMC-16853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbn